# OpenCode Environment Configuration
#
# Pre-configured inference via Serverless Inference (optional):
#   MODEL_ACCESS_KEY     Model access key (Inference > Manage in the control panel)
#   INFERENCE_MODEL      Inference model id from GET https://inference.do-ai.run/v1/models
#                        (OpenCode uses digitalocean/<id>). If empty, the first
#                        chat-capable model from that live list is used.
#   DO_INFERENCE_ROUTER  Optional. Name of a DigitalOcean Intelligent Inference
#                        Router attached to MODEL_ACCESS_KEY (in the control panel).
#                        If set, requests route through "router:<name>" using
#                        the SAME key and the router becomes the default.
# On first boot, 001_onboot reads /etc/environment first, then /opt/opencode.env.
# If MODEL_ACCESS_KEY is set in either place, Serverless Inference is configured
# and the interactive setup wizard is skipped on first login.
#
# Run the interactive setup script if these are empty:
#   /opt/setup-opencode.sh

MODEL_ACCESS_KEY=
INFERENCE_MODEL=
DO_INFERENCE_ROUTER=
